29,2,1,talk,Servas,,It seems our reporting processes are heavily dependent on the nature of the assets; physical goods provide a transparency that software simply cannot match.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The data suggests that our most stable returns and customer loyalty are tied to specific operational models, while others have proven far more volatile.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Minako,,"Our liquidity is under more pressure than we've admitted, and our ability to borrow is strictly limited to certain types of assets.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Mio,,"It looks like we have plenty of help for software, but finding people for physical operations is going to be a real challenge!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Deployment timelines vary wildly; some sectors face significant security hurdles, while hardware dependencies have caused substantial delays in the past.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,pass,Servas,,Skip,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
35,2,2,pass,Asuka,,Skip,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Minako,,We must be cautious about the type of security we can leverage if we need to maintain our cash flow.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Mio,,And we really need to consider if we have the bandwidth to manage the hiring for certain types of businesses!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Toshio,,I believe we should prioritize candidates that avoid both lengthy security reviews and the unpredictability of hardware supply chains.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Servas,,"I agree with Toshio, though I also believe we should favor companies whose performance we can verify independently to simplify our reporting.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we want to avoid the volatility I saw in the data, we should look for candidates with high customer retention and a proven exit profile.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Minako,,We should avoid any candidate that requires heavy follow-on capital or relies on assets that our current credit line doesn't recognize as security.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Mio,,I'll be voting for whoever doesn't need us to spend all our time hunting for specialized field crews or supervisors!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Toshio,,It seems we are all converging on a preference for stability and predictability over high-risk operational complexity.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Servas,,"Indeed, the wisdom of experience suggests that the simplest path to success is often the one with the fewest hidden obstacles.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Asuka,,Logic dictates that we prioritize a model that aligns with our successful exits and demonstrates resilience during price adjustments.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Minako,,I agree. We need a candidate that doesn't drain our reserves or leave us unable to secure funding when the next round comes.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Mio,,I'm just excited to see which one fits all these needs! I'll be ready to vote for the most balanced choice!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I believe we have a clear set of criteria now; let us see which candidate best avoids these operational and financial pitfalls.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
